# Root actions and software installs — always ask the user

Never work around missing software or missing privileges. If a task needs a
package installed or a root-only action (sysctl, mount, ptrace scope, gdb -p,
package install, ...), STOP and ask the user to run it — they have offered to
run root commands.

- Do NOT invent workarounds (stub headers, alternate tools, local builds that
  dodge the dependency, user-space reimplementations).
- Do NOT try to sudo from the agent shell.
- Ask with the exact command to run, e.g.:
  `clush -w fcstor0[03-15] yum install <pkg> -y`
- This applies to every node-side need: valgrind, libasan, gdb, strace,
  sysctls, /proc writes, capability changes.
